Package: kio-protondrive
Architecture: any
Depends:
  ${shlibs:Depends},
  ${misc:Depends}
Description: KIO worker for Proton Drive
 Browse, download, upload and manage files stored on Proton Drive directly
 from Dolphin (or any other KIO-aware application) via the protondrive://
 protocol. Files are fetched on demand, like sftp:// or Google Drive's
 kio-gdrive — there is no local sync/mirror.
 .
 This package only provides the KDE/Dolphin integration. It requires the
 official Proton Drive CLI ("proton-drive", from
 https://proton.me/drive/download) to be installed separately and
 authenticated ("proton-drive auth login") before protondrive:/ can be
 browsed.

Package: kio-protondrive-sync-daemon
Architecture: any
Section: net
Depends:
  ${shlibs:Depends},
  ${misc:Depends}
Recommends:
  libnotify-bin,
  kio-protondrive,
  kio-protondrive-wizard
Description: Background upload sync daemon for Proton Drive
 A systemd --user service that keeps locally-pinned Proton Drive files up
 to date. Right-click any file or folder under protondrive:/ in Dolphin
 to pin it: this downloads a local copy that the protondrive:// KIO
 worker then serves instantly (no CLI round-trip), and this daemon
 uploads any local edit to that copy back to Drive automatically, via the
 same "proton-drive" CLI used by the KIO worker. Unpinned files stay
 on-demand, fetched only when accessed.
 .
 One-way local -> Drive upload for pinned files only. Drive -> local
 sync (picking up remote changes made elsewhere) happens on next access,
 not via continuous background polling.

Package: kio-protondrive-wizard
Architecture: any
Depends:
  ${shlibs:Depends},
  ${misc:Depends},
  qml-qt6,
  qml6-module-org-kde-kirigami,
  qml6-module-qtcore,
  qml6-module-qtquick,
  qml6-module-qtquick-controls,
  qml6-module-qtquick-layouts,
  qml6-module-qtquick-window,
  qml6-module-qtquick-dialogs
Recommends:
  pass,
  gnupg
Description: First-run setup wizard for the Proton Drive sync daemon
 Graphical wizard that signs you in to Proton Drive and lets you choose
 how the background sync daemon stores your session (plain file vs.
 GPG-encrypted via pass). Launched automatically by
 kio-protondrive-sync-daemon when it needs authentication, or runnable
 manually.
 .
 Same architecture as this developer's linux-hello-rust project's own
 configuration GUI: a small Rust launcher spawning Qt's qml6 runtime for
 the interface, talking to it over a local control server — no compiled
 Qt/C++ code of its own.

Package: kio-protondrive-full
Architecture: all
Section: metapackages
Depends:
  kio-protondrive (= ${binary:Version}),
  kio-protondrive-sync-daemon (= ${binary:Version}),
  kio-protondrive-wizard (= ${binary:Version}),
  ${misc:Depends}
Description: KIO worker and background sync daemon for Proton Drive (metapackage)
 Umbrella package pulling in both the on-demand protondrive:// KIO worker
 (kio-protondrive) and the background upload sync daemon
 (kio-protondrive-sync-daemon), plus its first-run setup wizard
 (kio-protondrive-wizard). Installs no files of its own.
